---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<BaseLayout
  title="NO BALL GAMES Projects | Art, Lore, XRP Concepts & Street Culture"
  description="Explore NO BALL GAMES projects across Grime Art, digital collectibles, character lore, gaming concepts, clothing, community campaigns and XRP-side story work."
  current="projects"
>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <span class="eyebrow">Projects</span>
    <h1>A brand system with more than one lane.</h1>
    <p>
      NO BALL GAMES can expand across art, digital collectibles, gaming, clothing, events, community drops and story worlds. This page gives each lane a clear home while marking which claims are still concept-only.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section project-grid">
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">01 • Art</span>
      <h3>Street art and Grime Art archive</h3>
      <p>Paintings, walls, sketches, jackets, characters, signs and raw visual work connected to the NO BALL GAMES identity and Charlie Buster's Grime Art layer.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>See collections →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">02 • Collectibles</span>
      <h3>Digital collectible structure</h3>
      <p>A future-ready area for character drops, collector passes, burn mechanics, rarity pages and community rewards without overloading the homepage with unsupported token claims.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>View drops →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">03 • XRP / XRPL</span>
      <h3>XRP KIDs lore concept</h3>
      <p>The XRPL branch covers XRP KIDs, Alpha Aaron, FRET, $PMSL and Block Buster OG as a lore and digital-collectible concept. Verify issuer, collection and ledger data before treating any asset details as live fact.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}xrp/`}>Open the XRP page →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">04 • Gaming</span>
      <h3>Play against the rules</h3>
      <p>Mini-games, Telegram games, browser games, scoreboards, quests and community competitions can all sit under the same rebel-play concept.</p>
      <div class="coming-soon-tag">Coming soon</div>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">05 • Clothing</span>
      <h3>Wearable street culture</h3>
      <p>Hand-painted jackets, denim, patches, prints, stencil pieces and future apparel drops presented as premium limited releases.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}collections/`}>Browse wearables →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">06 • Lore</span>
      <h3>Characters and world-building</h3>
      <p>The sign becomes a mythology: characters, gangs, estates, courts, blocked zones, secret games and coded messages.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}lore/`}>Enter the lore →</a>
    </article>
    <article class="feature-card">
      <span class="kicker">07 • Community</span>
      <h3>Fans, collectors and creators</h3>
      <p>Community challenges, artist callouts, collector spotlights, collabs and local culture keep the brand active between major drops.</p>
      <a class="inline-link" href={`${base}community/`}>Join in →</a>
    </article>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="section-header">
      <h2>What is live now</h2>
      <p>Current status across all project lanes.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="status-grid">
      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status-label">Brand hub website</span>
        <span class="status-badge status-live">Live</span>
      </div>
      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status-label">Lore archive</span>
        <span class="status-badge status-live">Active</span>
      </div>
      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status-label">Research truth files</span>
        <span class="status-badge status-live">Active</span>
      </div>
      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status-label">XRP lore page</span>
        <span class="status-badge status-live">Live</span>
      </div>
      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status-label">Character drops</span>
        <span class="status-badge status-soon">Coming soon</span>
      </div>
      <div class="status-row">
        <span class="status-label">Gaming layer</span>
        <span class="status-badge status-soon">Coming soon</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section split-grid">
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Collaborate</span>
      <h2>Want to build something with us?</h2>
      <p>Artists, developers, collectors, writers and brand partners are welcome. The right collaborations get the best projects off the ground faster.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="button primary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Get in touch</a>
      </div>
    </article>
    <article class="panel-card">
      <span class="kicker">Brand notes</span>
      <ul class="list-clean">
        <li>Every project connects back to the core NO BALL GAMES identity.</li>
        <li>Grime Art is the visual language; NO BALL GAMES is one of the worlds it can build.</li>
        <li>XRPL lore pages should stay transparent about what is canon versus what is verified on-chain.</li>
        <li>Community and collector value comes before hype.</li>
      </ul>
    </article>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
